                <divLine xml:id="m-c9a2ec77-bd09-4cb5-936c-4e65dde9f224" facs="#m-38df3ede-4897-4303-bc5b-d11a6e38efea" form="finalis" />
              </layer>
            </staff>
            <div xml:id="m-3afd0eb3-a747-4dea-91c2-d3648b6c45e5">
              <lg xml:id="m-735f61c2-e24d-4c42-ae68-93df0ebb6d3c">
                <l xml:id="m-b5d2ef43-fb79-4da9-a018-c4bd8b46b7be" facs="#m-bbadba10-378c-44d6-8a7e-29c1b57643a6" label="text-like">Tones for the Y. « Benedicamus Domino».</l><l xml:id="m-ca4e9c18-609b-4098-99ba-37d0dc3c2f3c" facs="#m-db1bad1d-229d-4e68-a3bf-71d7a7f65e1a" label="ambiguous">127</l><l xml:id="m-57cce562-9452-48dc-8a97-91303f86e81c" facs="#m-4b59714b-7a3a-4fd0-84e4-6e10419588f3" label="text-like">VIII. — On the Sundays of Advent and Lent.</l><l xml:id="m-0710f1ab-0780-4beb-97dc-3793c40116a6" facs="#m-3a2b86f7-59f9-40cb-9fa3-feb9f9525c1a" label="ambiguous">6.</l><l xml:id="m-a7d514a5-5d9d-4e61-9062-91899fea4339" facs="#m-d49c5bfb-8498-426d-9174-7a0e97756522" label="lyrics-like">DEnedi-cá-mus Dó¬</l><l xml:id="m-a5cf8fb3-9d30-470a-95f3-a318c91ee430" facs="#m-d623ed21-121c-4490-bf8f-df61b9f1b44d" label="ambiguous">mi-no.</l><l xml:id="m-f75133d0-fd81-4d17-a4d7-528c2dd25cd1" facs="#m-86d90a2a-8e7d-4ec8-8387-7475e7d2e7ba" label="lyrics-like">N. Dé¬  grá¬</l><l xml:id="m-6c7f422c-27ae-4bf6-8314-88ba7d18c3a9" facs="#m-dd8da053-bc04-419a-9fb8-59080dc54c87" label="ambiguous">ti-as.</l><l xml:id="m-bacd6e62-5e75-46f7-b3cb-554cc5c66aac" facs="#m-0889d4a9-1492-42e8-9162-acb4b0fa688b" label="text-like">IX. — On the Sundays of Paschal Time.</l><l xml:id="m-fced6b05-8a84-472e-aab1-6710952146d4" facs="#m-16fdff79-30cd-431b-a985-89537a192d45" label="text-like">(In the Office of the Time.)</l><l xml:id="m-38600d6f-a459-448e-b308-b5bb7049b589" facs="#m-c2e6de97-e863-4c1d-8e91-2c84181ef276" label="ambiguous">7.</l><l xml:id="m-d500a340-91df-4758-a02c-d6edd5f54dab" facs="#m-c3129f5b-1e8e-4f9c-a731-9b3042acd50f" label="lyrics-like">Enedicámus Dó¬</l><l xml:id="m-0a592d83-b133-44ef-baac-0ae0abcbd05b" facs="#m-4371b225-81d1-4e6b-bf72-01df3ba7fa34" label="ambiguous">mino.</l><l xml:id="m-eabb7b1c-9537-452d-a5e6-577239bc9ea9" facs="#m-d21e9a05-0b51-412d-af2b-6cf26b93714d" label="lyrics-like">R. Dé¬o</l><l xml:id="m-ab30a122-f81a-451e-9052-b7c775a0cc9b" facs="#m-52c4d127-1fd3-473d-a66f-27f4c0d4aaaf" label="lyrics-like">grá-ti-as.</l><l xml:id="m-0d1b7a70-5c37-4be3-8d4b-f69d620a51f6" facs="#m-ad97dc0c-1566-4736-b415-554987adf5f7" label="lyrics-like">At Terce, before Pontifical Mass, the V. Benedicámus Dómino. is sung in</l><l xml:id="m-3d1cd4fe-5a73-49d6-9dc6-52f67bb65d32" facs="#m-873c9272-b028-472e-84e4-fb44b8e99af0" label="text-like">one of the preceding tones, for instance that of Lauds for feasts of the II class.</l><l xml:id="m-9c651afc-468d-484f-b98c-903b4de1f75c" facs="#m-5204dafc-d40b-48f6-93a5-32c521d3cb4b" label="text-like">Hypermetric Syllables in the Hymns.</l><l xml:id="m-86f8838e-adbd-4dee-9840-81798e4d00da" facs="#m-a6227291-c8a5-454f-80fb-e892147e88f7" label="text-like">According to a decree of the S. C. of Rites, dated May 14th 1915.</l><l xml:id="m-5331bf9a-c68c-4593-9c16-7e3d21383c7c" facs="#m-39556998-3a52-4624-8d71-1e8de55b268d" label="text-like">hypermetric or redundant syllables in the Hymns may be elided,</l><l xml:id="m-c7433adf-1c4b-4bd8-a997-4e161c27b396" facs="#m-79c4083e-4dcf-40d3-8409-e43ef550ba1f" label="text-like">if this method of interpretation be considered casier or more fitting.</l><l xml:id="m-f902c4e4-4d8d-4dc6-bc09-a4c83f154c17" facs="#m-0e89d09f-6e01-4bf8-9cde-709371c962ab" label="ambiguous">Two methods are therefore allowed:</l><l xml:id="m-d90199ae-5d9c-4a44-8a1e-3d3996f0c0a9" facs="#m-2c854b5c-9602-4277-9378-7089baedc36f" label="text-like">etther (a) the pronunciation of the hypermetric syllable, by giving it</l><l xml:id="m-3dd59ecd-4914-47d5-bf02-beec75f5bc00" facs="#m-a70ce60c-2dfd-4cd3-acaf-e5ec17238cd8" label="text-like">the separate note allotted to it in the notation, according</l><l xml:id="m-02b4d1d9-aa68-4165-9f2a-627c750abaa4" facs="#m-d3fd4428-9f0e-439d-b154-6b95f4d2308d" label="text-like">to the rules indicated in the official edition of the Roman</l><l xml:id="m-f3be560a-b534-4e3f-8a8e-9243b063094f" facs="#m-763ea504-6907-4f05-b11d-b905094fa95f" label="ambiguous">Antiphonary.</l><l xml:id="m-44a58c96-5d7a-42f5-88f4-fbeadfe9b60f" facs="#m-23bfa3b3-de15-4884-8f42-4035c7d372e8" label="text-like">)the suppression of the hypermetric syllable by elision, thus</l><l xml:id="m-9f43b156-1725-4f48-94cb-194707312af9" facs="#m-27bdfa89-7051-4428-93d1-2151ad7bad45" label="text-like">keeping the ordinary melodic formula.</l><l xml:id="m-76e2ac3e-0440-4bfd-8887-1f1cd9eb8867" facs="#m-f31b2bbb-7326-4db8-90b5-02bf4e71772f" label="ambiguous">Hypermetric syllables are printed in italics in our editions</l><l xml:id="m-8e63f1a1-5be5-4bea-8e6f-f66269518632" facs="#m-40ed3f60-548d-414b-a696-725765565eef" label="ambiguous">e. g. Cum Patre et almo Spiritu.</l></lg>
            </div>
          </section>
        </score>
      </mdiv>
    </body>
  </music>
</mei>